<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.14.5: Identifying Key Features of Graphed Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01997</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.14.5: Identifying Key Features of Graphed Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6d6b8075-24a0-463a-96a4-cfb54d5b32ea</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The equation \(y=(-16t−2)(t−1)\) represents the height in feet of a beach ball thrown by a child as a function of time, \(t\), in seconds.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Since the equation is in factored form, we can tell that the graph intersects the horizontal axis at two points. Use this information to find the zeros of the function. Explain or show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="bff14462-c156-487b-a781-d7d949799219" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="85f3be41-8f3f-4c2c-b8ea-ca5a6d375ec3" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-0.125">
    <problem>
      <para> Find one of the zeros of the functions using \((-16t−2)\). </para>
        <para>Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -0.125 or \(-\frac{1}{8}\). From the factored form, we can tell that the graph intersects the horizontal axis at \(t=-0.125\) or \(-\frac{1}{8}\). The zero of the function is the same value.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
